# Secrets and env files — MUST NOT enter the build context.
# Nested patterns (**/) are required: bare `.env.*` matches only the context
# root, so frontend/.env.local would otherwise leak into the Stage-1 frontend
# build. That file sets NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE=http://localhost:8000 for `next dev`;
# baking it into the production export hardcodes the API/SSE origin to
# localhost:8000, which breaks same-origin serving anywhere the browser's
# localhost is not the app (E2E compose network, cloud deploys). Excluding it
# lets `npm run build` fall back to the relative-URL default (NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE="").
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
# VCS
.git
.gitignore
# GSD planning artifacts
.planning
.claude
# Python bytecode and virtualenvs
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.venv
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.coverage
**/htmlcov
# Frontend caches (Stage 1 rebuilds these from scratch)
**/node_modules
frontend/.next
frontend/out
# Committed frontend export — Stage 1 regenerates it into the image. If the
# stale committed copy entered the context, `COPY backend/ /app/backend/` would
# land it at /app/backend/static and the later `COPY --from=frontend /build/out`
# would MERGE (not replace) over it, leaving orphaned stale chunks (e.g. an old
# bundle with a hardcoded localhost:8000 API origin) alongside the fresh export.
backend/static
# SQLite runtime artifact (must not be baked into image)
db/*.db
db/*.db-journal
# macOS/Editor junk
**/.DS_Store
**/*.log
# Test infra
test
